WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.092
A car repair. A vet bill.

2
00:00:03.172 --> 00:00:05.021
A gap between jobs.

3
00:00:05.101 --> 00:00:06.876
Surprises happen.

4
00:00:06.956 --> 00:00:10.487
A cash cushion keeps them
from turning into debt.

5
00:00:11.787 --> 00:00:19.458
In a Federal Reserve survey for 2025, 63%
of adults said they would cover a surprise

6
00:00:19.498 --> 00:00:23.363
$400 expense with cash or its equivalent.

7
00:00:23.443 --> 00:00:27.247
So more than a third would
have to borrow, sell something,

8
00:00:27.287 --> 00:00:29.292
or couldn't pay it right away.

9
00:00:30.592 --> 00:00:34.470
A cushion is money set
aside only for surprises.

10
00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:38.842
When something breaks, you pay from
the cushion instead of a credit card.

11
00:00:38.922 --> 00:00:42.286
Then you refill it,
one paycheck at a time.

12
00:00:43.586 --> 00:00:45.154
Why not invest it?

13
00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:48.828
Because you might need it
right when prices are down.

14
00:00:48.908 --> 00:00:51.811
Picture a $1,000 cushion.

15
00:00:51.891 --> 00:00:55.451
In savings, it's still $1,000.

16
00:00:55.531 --> 00:01:00.292
Invested, a 20% drop would leave $800.

17
00:01:00.372 --> 00:01:03.284
Stock prices can drop at any time,

18
00:01:03.324 --> 00:01:07.625
which is why money needed soon
is often kept in savings instead.

19
00:01:08.925 --> 00:01:13.416
Your first target can be small:
one month of must-pay costs.

20
00:01:13.496 --> 00:01:19.736
If rent, food, transport and minimum
debt payments add up to $1,800,

21
00:01:19.776 --> 00:01:21.260
that's your goal.

22
00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:26.099
Saving $150 a month gets
you there in 12 months.

23
00:01:27.399 --> 00:01:28.818
Quick recap.

24
00:01:28.898 --> 00:01:32.282
A cushion covers surprises
so they don't become debt.

25
00:01:32.362 --> 00:01:36.307
Money you may need soon has no
time to recover from a drop.

26
00:01:36.387 --> 00:01:40.425
And you can start small: even
one month of costs helps.

27
00:01:41.725 --> 00:01:42.770
Quick check.

28
00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:45.389
What is an emergency cushion for?

29
00:01:45.469 --> 00:01:49.924
Answer three short questions below
the video to finish the lesson.

30
00:01:51.224 --> 00:01:55.234
Now open your Money Map and add
up one month of must-pay costs.

31
00:01:55.314 --> 00:01:57.654
That's your first cushion target.
